Melatonin is a natural hormone produced by the pineal gland - a small organ located near the center of the brain. Melatonin regulates the sleep-wake cycle of the human brain.

Melatonin is produced artificially to cure disorders caused by the melatonin insufficiency or its improper secretion.

Reasons to take melatonin include:

- Troubles with falling asleep;

- Shift-work;

- Jet lag;

- Sleep disorders in blind people;

- Endometriosis; and

- Insomnia caused by beta-blockers (hypertension drugs).

Average dose of melatonin for adults ranges between 0.5-10 mg. The harmful effects of melatonin begin to dominate at around 30 mg - however, this maximum dosage threshold might differ in individual cases.

Melatonin side effects 📍

Melatonin shouldn't cause any side effects when used properly; however, it is essential to know the max dose of melatonin and lookout for all the alarming symptoms listed below.

- Signs of allergic reaction: swelling of your body parts (especially face), hives, trouble breathing - call for help immediately!

- Drowsiness;

- Increased sweating;

- Weird dreams;

- Feeling irritable, depressed mood, mood shifting;

- Stomach pain, headache; and

- Dizziness.

